# Allowlist, not a denylist: everything is excluded and the four paths the
# image build actually needs are added back. A denylist would ship whatever
# a developer happens to leave in the tree (a .env, a kubeconfig, a key)
# into the build context and into buildx's provenance attestation, and it
# would grow stale as the repo does.
#
# Before this file the context was ~1.1 GB, because `runs/` holds 204
# recorded evaluation runs and the repo root carries built binaries.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal
